# Files the Vercel CLI would otherwise upload into the build container.
#
# .env matters most: it was being uploaded, so the build logged "Detected .env
# file" and the Prisma CLI loaded the LOCAL connection string from it. Anything
# invoking `prisma` during a build then resolved DATABASE_URL from this file
# rather than the platform's real value. Vercel already injects the real
# DATABASE_URL and friends as environment variables, so shipping the local file
# only adds a leaked dev secret and a wrong default.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local runtime artefacts — large, and useless to a build.
db/
*.db
*.db-journal
dev.log
dev.out.log
server.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Screenshot/reference material that is not part of the site.
download/
examples/
t4.html
prev.html